---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
---

<Page
  path="/power/"
  title="Power | kiln-vm"
  description="A kiln-vm power mode decides whether a VM starts with the daemon, whether a command can wake it, and whether it stops when idle."
>
  <Fragment slot="open">
    <div class="say">
      <div class="say__lead">
        <h1 class="say__title">Power</h1>
        <pre class="cmd">kiln-vm power dev --mode on_demand --idle 10m</pre>
      </div>
      <p class="say__text">
        A power mode decides when a VM runs. Under <code>manual</code>, the default, you start and stop it yourself,
        and a stopped VM refuses commands. The other three modes do some of that for you.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="idle" aria-hidden="true">
      <p class="form form--cold">idle</p>
      <p class="form form--lit">idle</p>
    </div>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="ground">
    <div class="notes">
      <section class="note">
        <h2 class="note__title">on_demand</h2>
        <p>
          Stopped until a command needs it. <code>exec</code>, <code>shell</code>, <code>forward</code>, an upload or a
          download wakes it. It stops again after ten idle minutes, or the time you give <code>--idle</code>.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section class="note">
        <h2 class="note__title">warm</h2>
        <p>
          Starts with the daemon, so it is running before the first command. After that it stops when idle and wakes
          on use, like on_demand.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section class="note note--end">
        <h2 class="note__title">always</h2>
        <p>
          Starts with the daemon and never stops for being idle. Traffic and processes inside a guest don't count as
          use, so a VM that only serves requests needs this mode to stay up.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</Page>

<style>
  .idle {
    --lamp-width: 0.26em;
    --lamp-height: 0.3em;
    display: grid;
  }

  .idle .form {
    --fit: 1.806;
    --bearing: 0.063em;
    grid-area: 1 / 1;
  }

  .idle .form--cold {
    -webkit-mask:
      linear-gradient(#000 0 0),
      linear-gradient(#000 0 0) 0 0 / var(--lamp-width) var(--lamp-height) no-repeat;
    -webkit-mask-composite: xor;
    mask:
      linear-gradient(#000 0 0),
      linear-gradient(#000 0 0) 0 0 / var(--lamp-width) var(--lamp-height) no-repeat;
    mask-composite: exclude;
  }

  .idle .form--lit {
    clip-path: inset(0 calc(100% - var(--lamp-width)) calc(100% - var(--lamp-height)) 0);
  }
</style>
